# Product domain model for the simple Tundra interview website.
# Dogfood: session lifecycle, not UI/LLM vendor details.

tundra: Tundra interview session

roles:
  - Author
  - Facilitator

relationships:
  - Author is Owner of Session
  - Author is Owner of Model draft
  - Facilitator is Interviewer of Session

contracts:
  - Only the Author may start a Session and provide domain descriptions
  - The Facilitator must reframe the Author’s intent as a draft Tundra model and must not invent Roles, Contracts, States, Processes, or thresholds the Author did not state or strongly imply
  - A Model draft may be marked Structurally valid only after it passes the Tundra structural schema check
  - A Model draft may be marked Domain ready only when it is Structurally valid and has no unresolved testability gaps the Author still needs to answer
  - Only the Author may request Export of a Model draft
  - A Model draft may be Exported only when it is Domain ready
  - The Author may Abandon a Session at any time before Export
  - The Facilitator must close interview turns with an open question that invites correction or more detail, not a yes or no dead end

states:
  - Session is Open
  - Session is Awaiting Author input
  - Session is Abandoned
  - Model draft is Empty
  - Model draft is Proposed
  - Model draft is Structurally invalid
  - Model draft is Structurally valid
  - Model draft is Domain ready
  - Model draft is Exported

processes:
  - name: Start Session
    actor: Author
    requires: no Session exists
    results:
      - Session is Open
      - Model draft is Empty

  - name: Reframe as draft model
    actor: Facilitator
    requires: Session is Open
    results:
      - Model draft is Proposed
      - Session is Awaiting Author input

  - name: Author corrects or elaborates
    actor: Author
    requires: Session is Awaiting Author input
    results: Session is Open

  - name: Revise draft model
    actor: Facilitator
    requires: Session is Open
    results:
      - Model draft is Proposed
      - Session is Awaiting Author input

  - name: Run structural validation
    actor: System
    requires: Model draft is Proposed
    results:
      - Model draft is Structurally valid
      - Model draft is Structurally invalid

  - name: Resolve domain gaps
    actor: Author
    requires: Model draft is Structurally valid
    results: Model draft is Domain ready

  - name: Export model
    actor: Author
    requires: Model draft is Domain ready
    results: Model draft is Exported

  - name: Abandon Session
    actor: Author
    requires:
      - Session is Open
      - Session is Awaiting Author input
    results: Session is Abandoned

scenarios:
  - name: "Happy path: interview, validate, export"
    steps:
      - Given no Session exists
      - When the Author starts a Session
      - Then the Session is Open
      - And the Model draft is Empty
      - When the Author describes a business process
      - And the Facilitator reframes it as a draft model
      - Then the Model draft is Proposed
      - And the Session is Awaiting Author input
      - When the Author corrects or elaborates
      - And the Facilitator revises the draft model
      - Then the Model draft is Proposed
      - When the System runs structural validation successfully
      - Then the Model draft is Structurally valid
      - When the Author resolves remaining domain gaps
      - Then the Model draft is Domain ready
      - When the Author exports the model
      - Then the Model draft is Exported

  - name: "Error: Facilitator invents a threshold"
    steps:
      - Given the Session is Open
      - And the Author has not stated a measurable threshold
      - When the Facilitator tries to reframe with an invented numeric Contract
      - Then the reframe is rejected
      - And the contract "The Facilitator must reframe the Author’s intent as a draft Tundra model and must not invent Roles, Contracts, States, Processes, or thresholds the Author did not state or strongly imply" is broken

  - name: "Error: export before domain ready"
    steps:
      - Given the Model draft is Structurally valid
      - And domain gaps remain unresolved
      - When the Author tries to export the model
      - Then the export is rejected
      - And the contract "A Model draft may be Exported only when it is Domain ready" is broken

  - name: "Error: structural validation fails"
    steps:
      - Given the Model draft is Proposed
      - When the System runs structural validation and the schema check fails
      - Then the Model draft is Structurally invalid
      - And the contract "A Model draft may be marked Structurally valid only after it passes the Tundra structural schema check" is applied

  - name: "Author abandons before export"
    steps:
      - Given the Session is Open
      - When the Author abandons the Session
      - Then the Session is Abandoned
